# The findings of ShellCheck (severity warning) that .github/ci/shellcheck.sh lets pass, as it
# prints them without line and column: FILE: SEVERITY: MESSAGE [CODE]. Each with its reason; the
# list only shrinks (a finding fixed must leave it).

# /etc/rc.common sources the init scripts: it reads START, STOP and USE_PROCD and sets action
podkop/files/etc/init.d/podkop: warning: START appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally). [SC2034]
podkop/files/etc/init.d/podkop: warning: STOP appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally). [SC2034]
podkop/files/etc/init.d/podkop: warning: USE_PROCD appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally). [SC2034]
podkop/files/etc/init.d/podkop: warning: action is referenced but not assigned. [SC2154]
podkop/files/etc/init.d/podkop-early: warning: START appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally). [SC2034]

# a list of one service, on purpose: the shape of the loop of more
podkop/files/etc/uci-defaults/99-podkop: warning: This loop will only ever run once. Bad quoting or missing glob/expansion? [SC2043]

# as in itdoginfo/podkop: $timestamp is never set, the log line starts with a space
luci-app-podkop/root/etc/uci-defaults/50_luci-podkop: warning: timestamp is referenced but not assigned. [SC2154]

# the list of the files removed from Yacd split into words on purpose (no spaces in the names)
